<script>(function(){var P=[["Battle of Poitiers (1356)","/battle/battle-of-poitiers-1356","Battle","19 September 1356","An Anglo-Gascon army under Edward, the Black Prince, defeated a larger French army under King John II south of Poitiers in 1356, during the Hundred Years' War, and captured the king, which led to a truce and the Treaty of Brétigny."],["Battle of Alesia","/battle/battle-of-alesia","Battle","September 52 BCE","Julius Caesar's Roman army besieged the Gallic leader Vercingetorix and his allies in the fortified settlement of Alesia in September 52 BCE, beat off a Gallic relief force, and ended organised Gallic resistance."],["Battle of al-Qadisiyyah","/battle/battle-of-al-qadisiyyah","Battle","November 636","In November 636 the army of the Rashidun Caliphate defeated the Sasanian army of Rustam Farrokhzad at al-Qadisiyyah in Iraq, after which Ctesiphon fell and the Sasanians lost Mesopotamia."],["Battle of Hattin","/battle/battle-of-hattin","Battle","4 July 1187","On 4 July 1187 the army of the Crusader states, under King Guy of Jerusalem, was surrounded and broken near Tiberias by Saladin's forces, which then took Jerusalem and most Crusader-held towns and prompted the Third Crusade."],["Fall of Constantinople","/battle/fall-of-constantinople","Battle","6 April to 29 May 1453","The Ottoman army under Sultan Mehmed II besieged Constantinople for 53 days and took the Byzantine capital on 29 May 1453, after which the city was sacked and became the Ottoman capital; the fate of Emperor Constantine XI is unknown."],["Battle of Lake Trasimene","/battle/battle-of-lake-trasimene","Battle","21 June 217 BCE","Hannibal's Carthaginian army ambushed a Roman army under the consul Gaius Flaminius on the north shore of Lake Trasimene in 217 BCE, during the Second Punic War, and killed or captured nearly all of it."],["Battle of Isandlwana","/battle/battle-of-isandlwana","Battle","22 January 1879","A Zulu army of some 20,000 overran part of the British main column at Isandlwana in Zululand on 22 January 1879, early in the Anglo-Zulu War, killing over 1,300 troops and bringing a larger second British invasion."],["Battle of the Somme","/battle/battle-of-the-somme","Battle","1 July – 18 November 1916","British Empire and French armies attacked the German Second Army on both sides of the upper Somme from 1 July to 18 November 1916, gaining about 10 km at a cost of over a million casualties."],["Battle of Ayacucho","/battle/battle-of-ayacucho","Battle","9 December 1824","On the Pampa de Ayacucho in the Peruvian highlands, Antonio José de Sucre's United Liberation Army defeated the royalist army of Viceroy José de la Serna, who was wounded and captured, and the royalists capitulated, ending Spanish rule in Peru."],["Battle of Manzikert","/battle/battle-of-manzikert","Battle","26 August 1071","On 26 August 1071 the Seljuk army of Alp Arslan defeated the Byzantine army of Romanos IV Diogenes near Manzikert in eastern Anatolia and captured the emperor, and civil strife in Byzantium followed."],["Battle of Stalingrad","/battle/battle-of-stalingrad","Battle","17 July 1942 – 2 February 1943","The Soviet Union defeated Germany and its Axis allies at Stalingrad on the Volga between 1942 and 1943; the German 6th Army was encircled and surrendered, and the strategic initiative on the Eastern Front passed to the Red Army."],["Battle of Grunwald","/battle/battle-of-grunwald","Battle","15 July 1410","The Polish and Lithuanian army under Władysław II Jagiełło and Vytautas defeated the Teutonic Order under Grand Master Ulrich von Jungingen near Grunwald in 1410, killing him and much of the Order's leadership."],["Third Battle of Panipat","/battle/third-battle-of-panipat","Battle","14 January 1761","On 14 January 1761 the Durrani Empire and its Indian allies defeated the Maratha army at Panipat, 97 kilometres north of Delhi; tens of thousands of Marathas died in the fighting and after it."],["Battle of Cannae","/battle/battle-of-cannae","Battle","2 August 216 BCE","Hannibal's Carthaginian army surrounded and destroyed most of a larger Roman and allied army under the consuls Paullus and Varro at Cannae in Apulia in 216 BCE, during the Second Punic War."],["Battle of Leuctra","/battle/battle-of-leuctra","Battle","6 July 371 BCE","The Boeotians led by the Thebans defeated Sparta and its allies at Leuctra in Boeotia on 6 July 371 BCE, after a dispute over renewing the King's Peace, and Spartan influence over Greece was shattered."],["Battle of Marathon","/battle/battle-of-marathon","Battle","12 September 490 BCE","The Athenians, helped by Plataea, defeated a Persian force under Datis and Artaphernes on the plain of Marathon in Attica in 490 BCE, ending the first Persian invasion of Greece."],["Battles of Khalkhin Gol","/battle/battles-of-khalkhin-gol","Battle","11 May – 15 September 1939","Soviet and Mongolian forces under Georgy Zhukov fought Japanese and Manchukoan forces on the disputed Mongolia-Manchukuo border in 1939, and by 31 August had trapped and destroyed the Japanese forces on the Mongolian side."],["Battle of the Teutoburg Forest","/battle/battle-of-the-teutoburg-forest","Battle","8 to 11 September 9 CE","An alliance of Germanic peoples led by Arminius ambushed three Roman legions under Publius Quinctilius Varus in 9 CE, possibly near Kalkriese, and ended Roman expansion beyond the Rhine."],["Battle of Plataea","/battle/battle-of-plataea","Battle","August 479 BCE","In August 479 BCE a Spartan-led Greek alliance defeated the Achaemenid army of Mardonius near Plataea in Boeotia, killing Mardonius and trapping much of his army in its camp, which ended the second Persian invasion of Greece."],["Battle of Tsushima","/battle/battle-of-tsushima","Battle","27–28 May 1905","In the Tsushima Strait on 27–28 May 1905 the Japanese Combined Fleet under Tōgō Heihachirō destroyed or captured nearly all of the Russian Second Pacific Squadron under Rozhestvensky, and Russia sued for peace that year."],["Battle of Nagashino","/battle/battle-of-nagashino","Battle","29 June 1575","In June 1575 the allied armies of Oda Nobunaga and Tokugawa Ieyasu defeated Takeda Katsuyori's army near Nagashino Castle in Mikawa Province, Japan, killing many Takeda generals and making Nobunaga's unification of Japan seem certain."],["Battle of Okinawa","/battle/battle-of-okinawa","Battle","1 April – 22 June 1945","United States Army and Marine Corps forces invaded Okinawa on 1 April 1945 and, after 82 days against the Japanese Thirty-Second Army, took the island at a cost that fell most heavily on its Okinawan civilians."],["Battles of Lexington and Concord","/battle/battles-of-lexington-and-concord","Battle","19 April 1775","British regulars sent from Boston to seize military supplies at Concord fought Massachusetts militia at Lexington, Concord and along the road back on 19 April 1775, the first major fighting of the American Revolutionary War."],["Battle of Actium","/battle/battle-of-actium","Battle","2 September 31 BCE","Octavian's fleet under Marcus Agrippa defeated the combined fleets of Mark Antony and Cleopatra off Actium in the Ionian Sea in 31 BCE, after which both took their own lives and Octavian became sole master of Rome."],["Battle of Issus","/battle/battle-of-issus","Battle","5 November 333 BCE","Alexander the Great's Hellenic League army defeated the Achaemenid army of Darius III near the Pinarus river by Issus in southern Anatolia in 333 BCE, and Darius fled, leaving his family and treasury to be captured."],["Normandy landings","/battle/normandy-landings","Battle","6 June 1944","On 6 June 1944 American, British and Canadian forces, with airborne troops and a fleet drawn from eight navies, landed on five beaches on the Normandy coast, opening the liberation of France and Western Europe."],["Battle of Zama","/battle/battle-of-zama","Battle","202 BCE","A Roman army under Scipio Africanus defeated a Carthaginian army under Hannibal near Zama in what is now Tunisia in 202 BCE, ending the Second Punic War and leaving Carthage politically subordinate to Rome."],["Battle of Uhud","/battle/battle-of-uhud","Battle","23 March 625","The Quraysh of Mecca under Abu Sufyan ibn Harb fought the early Muslims under Muhammad near Mount Uhud, north of Medina, in March 625; the Muslims lost heavily after part of their archer force left its hill, and the Meccans withdrew without pressing on."],["Battle of the Nile","/battle/battle-of-the-nile","Battle","1–3 August 1798","A British fleet under Rear-Admiral Sir Horatio Nelson attacked the French fleet of Vice-admiral Brueys anchored in Aboukir Bay, Egypt, in August 1798, and destroyed or captured all but four of its ships, leaving Napoleon's army in Egypt cut off."],["Battle of Puebla","/battle/battle-of-puebla","Battle","5 May 1862","French troops under Charles de Lorencez failed three times to storm the Mexican forts of Loreto and Guadalupe above Puebla on 5 May 1862, during the second French intervention in Mexico, and withdrew to Orizaba to await reinforcements."],["Siege of Jerusalem (1099)","/battle/siege-of-jerusalem-1099","Battle","7 June – 15 July 1099","Crusaders from Western Europe besieged Fatimid-held Jerusalem from 7 June to 15 July 1099, took it by assault with siege towers and a ram, massacred thousands of its people, and soon founded the Kingdom of Jerusalem."],["Battle of the Pyramids","/battle/battle-of-the-pyramids","Battle","21 July 1798","On 21 July 1798 Bonaparte's French army, formed in squares, defeated Murad Bey's Mamluk-led force near Embabeh in Ottoman Egypt, shattering Murad's field army and opening the way to Cairo."],["Battle of Ain Jalut","/battle/battle-of-ain-jalut","Battle","3 September 1260","On 3 September 1260 the Bahri Mamluks of Egypt under Sultan Qutuz defeated a Mongol force of the Ilkhanate under Kitbuqa at Ain Jalut in the Jezreel Valley, and the Mamluks then took Damascus and Aleppo."],["Battle of Tarawa","/battle/battle-of-tarawa","Battle","20–23 November 1943","United States Marines landed on Betio, the main island of Tarawa Atoll in the Gilbert Islands, on 20 November 1943 and took it from its Japanese garrison in 76 hours at a cost of nearly 6,400 lives on all sides."],["Battle of the Trebia","/battle/battle-of-the-trebia","Battle","22 or 23 December 218 BCE","Hannibal's Carthaginian army lured a Roman army under the consul Sempronius Longus across the icy Trebia near Placentia in December 218 BCE, in the first major battle of the Second Punic War, and defeated it heavily."],["Battle of Salamis","/battle/battle-of-salamis","Battle","480 BCE","An Allied Greek fleet under Themistocles defeated a larger Achaemenid fleet under King Xerxes in the straits between the island of Salamis and the mainland in 480 BCE, after which Xerxes withdrew with much of his army."],["Fall of Singapore","/battle/fall-of-singapore","Battle","8 to 15 February 1942","Japanese forces under General Tomoyuki Yamashita crossed the Johor Strait and took Singapore from the British garrison under Lieutenant-General Arthur Percival, who surrendered on 15 February 1942 in the Second World War."],["Battle of Kadesh","/battle/battle-of-kadesh","Battle","May 1274 BCE","Ramesses II of Egypt and Muwatalli II of the Hittite Empire fought on the Orontes near Kadesh after a Hittite attack nearly broke the Egyptian army; both sides claimed victory and the Hittites kept Kadesh."],["Battle of Jena–Auerstedt","/battle/battle-of-jena-auerstedt","Battle","14 October 1806","On 14 October 1806 Napoleon's army defeated Prince Hohenlohe's Prussians at Jena while Marshal Davout's single corps beat the main Prussian army at Auerstedt, in the War of the Fourth Coalition; Prussia's resistance collapsed in the weeks after."],["Battle of the Little Bighorn","/battle/battle-of-the-little-bighorn","Battle","25–26 June 1876","On the Little Bighorn River in Montana Territory, Lakota, Northern Cheyenne and Arapaho forces defeated the 7th Cavalry under Lieutenant Colonel Custer in June 1876, the most significant action of the Great Sioux War, which the United States still won."],["Battle of Raphia","/battle/battle-of-raphia","Battle","22 June 217 BCE","Ptolemy IV of Egypt defeated Antiochus III of the Seleucid Empire near Raphia on 22 June 217 BCE, in the Fourth Syrian War, and kept Coele-Syria for Egypt until Antiochus took it back at Panium in 200 BCE."],["Battle of Gaugamela","/battle/battle-of-gaugamela","Battle","1 October 331 BCE","Alexander the Great and the army of Macedon defeated the Persian army of Darius III at Gaugamela, north of Arbela in what is now Iraq, in 331 BCE; the Achaemenid Empire fell soon after."],["Battle of Shanghai","/battle/battle-of-shanghai","Battle","13 August – 26 November 1937","China's National Revolutionary Army and Japan's Imperial Army fought for Shanghai from August to November 1937, in the Second Sino-Japanese War; Japan took the city at heavy cost to both sides and advanced on Nanjing."],["Battle of the Granicus","/battle/battle-of-the-granicus","Battle","May 334 BCE","In May 334 BCE Alexander the Great of Macedon defeated the field army of the Persian satraps of Asia Minor at the crossing of the Granicus in the Troad, the first of his three major battles with the Achaemenid Empire."],["Battle of San Jacinto","/battle/battle-of-san-jacinto","Battle","21 April 1836","A Texian army under Sam Houston defeated Antonio López de Santa Anna's Mexican force in about 18 minutes at San Jacinto in Texas on 21 April 1836, the last battle of the Texas Revolution, and Santa Anna was captured the next day."],["Battle of Iwo Jima","/battle/battle-of-iwo-jima","Battle","19 February – 26 March 1945","American Marines, Navy and Army forces landed on Iwo Jima in the Volcano Islands in February 1945 and took it from the Japanese garrison under Kuribayashi in five weeks, at a cost in casualties higher than the Japanese suffered."],["Battle of Sekigahara","/battle/battle-of-sekigahara","Battle","21 October 1600 (Keichō 5, 15th day of the 9th month)","On 21 October 1600 the forces of Tokugawa Ieyasu defeated a coalition led by Ishida Mitsunari in what is now Gifu Prefecture after several commanders defected; Ieyasu became shōgun in 1603."],["Battle of Poltava","/battle/battle-of-poltava","Battle","8 July 1709","A Russian army under Tsar Peter I defeated a Swedish army commanded by Carl Gustaf Rehnskiöld near Poltava in Ukraine on 8 July 1709, the largest battle of the Great Northern War; the rest of the Swedish army surrendered three days later."],["Fall of Tenochtitlan","/battle/fall-of-tenochtitlan","Battle","May – 13 August 1521","A Spanish force under Hernán Cortés and tens of thousands of Indigenous allies, above all Tlaxcalans, besieged the Mexica capital Tenochtitlan in 1521, starved it, and took it on 13 August, after which the city was sacked."],["Battle of Badr","/battle/battle-of-badr","Battle","13 March 624 CE","On 13 March 624 CE (17 Ramadan, 2 AH) Muhammad's followers from Medina defeated a larger Qurayshi army from Mecca near Badr, killing several Meccan leaders and strengthening Muhammad's position."],["Battle of Waterloo","/battle/battle-of-waterloo","Battle","18 June 1815","On 18 June 1815 a French army under Napoleon was defeated near Waterloo, in present-day Belgium, by a British-led army under Wellington and a Prussian army under Blücher; Napoleon abdicated again four days later."],["Battle of Dien Bien Phu","/battle/battle-of-dien-bien-phu","Battle","13 March – 7 May 1954","Viet Minh forces under Võ Nguyên Giáp besieged and overran a French Union garrison in the valley of Điện Biên Phủ in northwest Tonkin in 1954, in the First Indochina War, and French withdrawal from Indochina followed."],["Battle of the Hydaspes","/battle/battle-of-the-hydaspes","Battle","May 326 BCE","Alexander the Great's Macedonian army crossed the swollen Hydaspes in May 326 BCE and defeated the Pauravas under Porus on its bank in what is now Punjab, Pakistan; Alexander spared Porus and made him a satrap."],["Battle of Crécy","/battle/battle-of-crecy","Battle","26 August 1346","An English army under Edward III, standing on a hillside near Crécy-en-Ponthieu in northern France, beat off repeated attacks by a much larger French army under Philip VI in 1346, during the Hundred Years' War, and went on to take Calais."],["Battle of Midway","/battle/battle-of-midway","Battle","4–7 June 1942","Two United States carrier groups sank all four Japanese fleet carriers present near Midway Atoll in June 1942, six months after Pearl Harbor, and wrecked Admiral Yamamoto's plan to capture the atoll and destroy the American carriers."],["Battle of Karbala","/battle/battle-of-karbala","Battle","10 October 680","On 10 October 680 at Karbala in southern Iraq, the army of the Umayyad caliph Yazid I killed Husayn ibn Ali, grandson of Muhammad, and most of his small party, with consequences for the Second Fitna and for Shia identity."],["Battle of Verdun","/battle/battle-of-verdun","Battle","21 February – 18 December 1916","The German 5th Army attacked the French defences at Verdun on the Western Front in 1916 to draw in and wear down the French army; after 302 days the French had recovered most of the ground and the Germans had failed to reach their aim."],["Battle of Carrhae","/battle/battle-of-carrhae","Battle","9 June 53 BCE","A Parthian cavalry army under Surena defeated the Roman army of Marcus Licinius Crassus near Carrhae in 53 BCE; Crassus was killed, most of his men were killed or captured, and Parthia later invaded Syria and Armenia."],["Battle of Austerlitz","/battle/battle-of-austerlitz","Battle","2 December 1805","Napoleon's Grande Armée defeated a combined Russian and Austrian army near Austerlitz in Moravia on 2 December 1805, in the War of the Third Coalition, and Austria then left the war by the Treaty of Pressburg."],["Battle of Leipzig","/battle/battle-of-leipzig","Battle","16–19 October 1813","The armies of the Sixth Coalition, from Austria, Prussia, Sweden and Russia, defeated Napoleon's Grande Armée at Leipzig in Saxony over four days in October 1813, and the French withdrew to France."]],d=Math.floor(Date.now()/864e5),p=P[d%P.length],a=document.getElementById("hub-pick");if(a){a.href=p[1];var im=document.createElement("img");im.src="/logos/thumbs/"+encodeURIComponent(p[0]).replace(/'/g,"%27")+".png";im.alt="";im.width=64;im.height=64;a.querySelector(".hub-pick-img").appendChild(im);a.querySelector(".hub-pick-k").textContent="Today\u2019s pick \u00b7 "+p[2]+(p[3]?" \u00b7 "+p[3]:"");a.querySelector(".hub-pick-n").textContent=p[0];a.querySelector(".hub-pick-d").textContent=p[4];}var b=document.getElementById("hub-surprise"),P=["/battle/"];if(b)b.addEventListener("click",function(){function go(){if(typeof SEARCH_PROFILES==="undefined")return;var a=SEARCH_PROFILES.filter(function(r){return P.some(function(p){return r[1].indexOf(p)===0})});if(a.length)location.href=a[Math.floor(Math.random()*a.length)][1]}if(typeof SEARCH_PROFILES!=="undefined")return go();var sc=document.createElement("script");sc.src=(typeof SEARCH_PROFILES_SRC!=="undefined"?SEARCH_PROFILES_SRC:"/search-profiles.js");sc.onload=go;sc.onerror=go;document.head.appendChild(sc)});})();</script>
